    "body": "## Summary\n- add a dedicated GPS capture-time freshness validator at the live-tracking API boundary\n- reduce replay exposure from the previous broad 10-minute service tolerance to a configurable 120-second maximum sample age\n- allow only a small configurable 30-second future clock-skew tolerance\n- cover exact boundaries, stale/future rejection and invalid configuration with deterministic unit tests\n- expose the limits through Spring configuration, Docker Compose and `.env.example`\n\n## Security rationale\nLive courier coordinates are short-lived operational data. Accepting substantially delayed device samples can move the marker backwards or replay an old route position even when sequence checks have no prior persisted sample. The API now rejects stale capture timestamps before they reach tracking persistence, while preserving a small tolerance for ordinary device clock skew.\n\n## Validation\n- branch is directly based on current `master` (`b9ebc684`)\n- diff reviewed: 6 files, no persistence schema changes and therefore no Flyway migration required\n- deterministic unit tests added for time-window boundaries\n- local dependency-backed execution is unavailable in this automation environment; GitHub CI and smoke workflows are the merge gate\n\nDo not merge unless available checks pass.",
